# Git LFS was previously enabled here with:
#     *.csv filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
#
# It was removed on 2026-10-03. Two reasons:
#
# 1. LFS stored a brand-new full-size object every time a CSV changed. Appending
#    one daily row to a 192 KB file uploaded all 192 KB again, for all 1,073
#    files, every day. Measured: 189 KB per file per day under LFS versus
#    0.24 KB with plain git - roughly 780x - because git deltas a changed file
#    against its previous version while LFS has no such concept. That had grown
#    .git/lfs to 7.1 GB for a 60 MB dataset.
#
# 2. This file was never committed. Git read it from the working tree at commit
#    time, so the repository stored LFS pointers, but a fresh clone had no
#    .gitattributes and therefore no LFS filter - so anyone cloning the repo
#    received 134-byte pointer stubs instead of CSV files. The dataset was
#    unusable outside the machine that produced it.
#
# The history was converted with `git lfs migrate export`, so every revision now
# holds real CSV content.